A restaurant-style honey sesame chicken made at home. First lightly seared in a cornstarch and egg batter, then slow-baked in a sticky, glossy honey-soy glaze that caramelizes into every bite.

*Adapted from [The Recipe Critic](https://therecipecritic.com/2013/09/baked-honey-sesame-chicken/).*

## Ingredients

### Chicken
- 4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts, cut into bite-sized pieces
- 1 cup cornstarch
- 3 large eggs, lightly beaten
- Salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- ¼ cup vegetable or canola oil (for searing)

### Honey Sesame Sauce
- ¾ cup honey
- ¾ cup soy sauce (low-sodium recommended)
- ½ cup ketchup
- ½ cup brown sugar
- ½ cup rice wine vinegar
- 1 teaspoon toasted sesame oil
- 1 teaspoon minced garlic
- 1 tablespoon cornstarch
- 1–2 tablespoons toasted sesame seeds (for garnish)
- 2 green onions, thinly sliced (optional, for garnish)

## Instructions

1. **Prep the Oven and Chicken:** Preheat your oven to 325°F (165°C). Lightly grease a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray. Cut chicken breasts into bite-sized chunks and season generously with salt and black pepper.
2. **Dredge:** Place the cornstarch in a gallon-sized ziplock bag (or shallow dish) and beaten eggs in a shallow bowl. Add chicken to the cornstarch and seal/shake to coat evenly. Shake off any excess cornstarch, then dip the coated pieces into the beaten eggs.
3. **Sear Until Golden:** Heat ¼ cup oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Working in batches so as not to crowd the skillet, cook chicken pieces for 2 to 3 minutes until golden brown on all sides (they do not need to be cooked through yet). Transfer the browned chicken into the prepared baking dish.
4. **Whisk the Sauce:** In a medium bowl, whisk together the honey, soy sauce, ketchup, brown sugar, rice wine vinegar, sesame oil, minced garlic, and 1 tablespoon cornstarch until completely blended.
5. **Bake and Baste:** Pour the sauce evenly over the chicken in the baking dish. Bake uncovered at 325°F for 45 minutes. Every 15 minutes, give the chicken a good stir with a spoon or spatula to turn and baste the pieces in the bubbling, thickening glaze.
6. **Garnish and Serve:** Remove from oven and let stand for 5 minutes to let the glaze thicken further. Sprinkle with toasted sesame seeds and sliced green onions. Serve over warm steamed jasmine rice or noodles.

## Notes

- **Ziplock Bag Method:** Tossing the chicken chunks with cornstarch in a gallon ziplock bag ensures an even coating with minimal mess.
- **Sauce Thickness:** The sauce will continue to thicken as it cools slightly after coming out of the oven.
